<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<SActionScript version="1" name="plugin_generic_editor_survives_strip">

  <!-- fix/editor-ui-and-shortcuts, issue (a), follow-up (2026-08-23): the
       NATIVE editor was fixed first, but the GENERIC (slider-list) editor
       had the IDENTICAL ownership bug and is very likely the window the
       original reporter actually saw — they are on Linux, and
       SPluginNativeEditor::attachPlugin() refuses a VST3 editor on X11
       (caps().needsRunLoop), so openParamEditor() falls through to the
       generic editor for EVERY VST3 instrument on that platform. Fixing only
       the native path left the field bug live.

       ROOT CAUSE: SPluginEffectStrip::ensureParamEditor() did
       `dlg = new QDialog(this)` — parented to the STRIP — and kept the
       QDialog in `editors_`, a MEMBER of the strip. STrackDetailPanel::
       rebuildUI()'s `delete pluginStrip_` on every track selection change
       therefore destroyed this editor too, exactly as it destroyed the
       native one, and for the identical reason.

       FIX: the dialog now parents to `window()` (the durable top-level
       ancestor, mirroring SPluginNativeEditor's own fix) and the registry
       moved to a MODULE-LEVEL map keyed by SPluginSlot* (genericEditorRegistry
       () in splugineffectstrip.cpp), mirroring SPluginNativeEditor::registry()
       — not a strip member, so it survives the strip that opened it.
       SPluginEffectStrip::isGenericEditorOpenFor()/closeGenericEditorFor() are
       the new static, symmetric query/close, added for exactly this gate.

       This case uses tw.test.clap.stereoskew, which has NO clap.gui
       (plugin_ui_strip_and_editor.qxa already gates that this fixture
       resolves to "generic", never "native"), so `open-via-strip` genuinely
       exercises ensureParamEditor()'s own parenting rather than falling
       through from a native attach failure.

       Watched failing on the pre-fix binary: expectOpen="1" read
       isGenericEditorOpenFor()==false after the throwaway strip was
       destroyed — the dialog died with it, same shape as the native gate. -->

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-sample trackIndex="0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav" timePos="0"/>

    <insert-plugin trackPath="0" slotIndex="0"
                   format="clap" uid="tw.test.clap.stereoskew"
                   name="Smaragd Test Stereo Skew" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>

    <!-- Confirms the fixture genuinely reaches the generic path (no native
         GUI to fall through from). -->
    <assert-plugin-editor-kind trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" expect="generic"/>

    <!-- Open through a throwaway strip, exactly as a track-switch rebuild
         would tear one down; the editor must survive. -->
    <plugin-generic-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0"
                           action="open-via-strip" expectOpen="1"/>

    <!-- Twice, not a one-shot survival. -->
    <plugin-generic-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0"
                           action="open-via-strip" expectOpen="1"/>

    <!-- Take it down. -->
    <plugin-generic-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0"
                           action="close" expectOpen="0"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="1"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
